# Crush 80 ZMK

Rules: `AGENTS.md` (hardware safety rules are binding). Procedures: `docs/guides/install-and-upgrade.md`, `docs/guides/recovery.md`. Current state: `docs/status.md`.

## Commands

- Build: `bash build.sh --skip-bridge` (RGB: add `--rgb`). Output in `dist/` (gitignored). Needs the west workspace; see `docs/guides/build.md`.
- Validate an image offline: `./crush80 check dist/crush80-zmk-app.signed.bin`
- Upgrade: `./crush80 update [IMAGE]` (or `bash update.sh`). Trial boot, host confirm.
- Hung or dead board: `./crush80 recover`
- Gate before commit: `bash scripts/gate/verify.sh`

## Layout

MCUboot 0x0-0xFFFF, slot 0 (app) 0x10000-0x7FFFF, slot 1 (upload/revert) 0x80000-0xEFFFF, protected 0xFE000+. `docs/features/flash-layout.md`.

## GPIO (confirmed from the stock firmware)

- Columns 0-15: PE0, PE1, PE2, PE4, PE5, PE6, PB0, PB1, PB2, PB3, PB4, PB5, PB6, PC0, PC1, PC4
- Rows 0-5: PD7, PD2, PD3, PD4, PD5, PD6
- RGB (Reboot Pro): PB7 = PSPI MOSI to the WS2812 chain, PC2 = LED power. `docs/features/rgb.md`.
- Battery ADC: PD1.

## Config source

`build.sh` picks the keymap from `CRUSH80_KEYMAP`, else `~/.config/DOTFILES/keybindings/crush80-zmk/`, else `keymaps/stock.keymap`. Edit the keymap there, not in `zmk/boards/crush80/crush80.keymap` (it is overwritten).

## Debugging

- SMP check: `./crush80 status`
- Kscan debugging: `CONFIG_ZMK_LOG_LEVEL_DBG=y`, never `LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL=4`.
